The following is a list of such of the Taddhita affixes as are commonly to be met with.

## Section I. Miscellaneous Affixes

### @deva[अ]

is added in the sense of:—

**(1)** 'the son of'; as @deva[उपगोः अपत्यं उपगव्यः] 'the son of Upagu'; so @deva[वाह्नेयः] from @deva[बह्नेय]; @deva[पर्वतस्य अपत्यं स्त्री पार्वती] 'the daughter of the mountain,' &c.

**(2)** ' the descendant of'; as @deva[उत्सस्य गोत्रप्रापयं पुमान् औत्सः] ' a descendant of Utsa', @deva[उत्सस्य गोत्रप्रापयं स्त्री औत्सी] 'a female descendant of Utsa', ( vide @ref[311], @ref[318] );

**(3)** ' dyed with,' @deva[हरिद्रया रक्तं हारिद्रं वस्त्रं] ' a garment dyed with turmeric';

**(4)** 'made of,' @deva[देवदारोर्विकारः देवदारवः] 'made of the fir tree;'

**(5)** 'belonging to,' &c.; @deva[देवस्य अयं देवः] 'belonging to a god,' @deva[शर्कराया भवं शार्करं] 'of sand'; @deva[ऊर्णाया भवं और्णं वस्त्रं] 'a woolen garment,' @deva[ग्रैष्मः] 'belonging to the sultry season'; @deva[नैशः] 'nocturnal;' @deva[सांवत्सरः] 'yearly' &c.; when added to @deva[हैमन्त] the final @deva[त] is dropped, @deva[हैमनः] 'autumnal,' ( vide Sis. VI. 65; Kir. XVII. 12 ). @deva[हैमन्तः] means 'agreeable in the autumnal season;'

**(6)** 'lord of'; @deva[पृथिव्या ईश्वरः पार्थिवः] 'the lord of the earth': @deva[पञ्चालानां स्वामी पाञ्चालः] 'the king of the Panchālas'; @deva[ऐक्ष्वाकः][^1] 'the king of the Ikshvāku race',

**(7)** 'a collection of'; @deva[काकानां समूहः काकं]; @deva[बकानां समूहः बाकं] 'a flock of cranes'; similarly @deva[मायूरं] from @deva[मयूर] 'a peacock,' @deva[कापोतं] from @deva[कपोत] 'a pigeon', @deva[शिखिनां समूहो शैखिनं]; @deva[गर्भिणीनां समूहो गार्भिणं] &c

**(8)** 'knowing or studying'; @deva[व्याकरणं अधीते वेद वा वैयाकरणः] 'one who studies grammar, grammarian', &c.

**(9)** and to form abstract nouns; @deva[मुनेः भावः मौनं] 'silence', @deva[युवन्-यौवनं] 'youth,' @deva[सुहृद्-सौहार्दं] 'friendship'; @deva[पृथोर्भावः पार्थवं] 'greatness, width,' &c.

### @deva[क]

forms derivatives with various significations:—

**(1)** @deva[उष्ट्रे भवः औष्ट्रकः] 'produced from or relating to a camel;' @deva[ग्रीष्मे भवः ग्रैष्मकः] 'produced in the hot season,'

**(2)** @deva[कुलालेन कृतं कौलालकं] 'made by a potter' @deva[ब्रह्मणा कृतं ब्राह्मकं] 'made by Brahman,'

**(3)** @deva[आरण्यकः] 'a forester,' 'a wild man',

**(4)** @deva[राज्ञां योग्यं राजन्यकं] 'a place fit for kings to live in'; @deva[मानुष्यकं] 'a country fit for men to live in' @deva[कुरुषु जातः कौरवकः] (also @deva[कौरवः][^2]) 'an inhabitant of Kuru'; @deva[युगन्धरेषु जातः यौगन्धरकः] (also @deva[यौगन्धरः][^2]) 'inhabiting Yugandhara';

**(6)** @deva[पथि जातं पन्थ्यकं] 'grown on a way';

**(7)** @deva[पन्थानं गच्छतीति पथिकः] 'a traveller';

**(8)** @deva[पूर्वाह्णे भवः पूर्वाह्णिकः] 'happening in the forenoon'; similarly @deva[अपराह्णिकः] 'happening in the afternoon',

**(9)** is added to denote 'enmity' @deva[काकोलूकयोः वैरं काकोलूकिका][^3] 'the antipathy between the crow and the owl'; similarly @deva[कुत्सिकुटिलिका], &c.;

**(10)** when added to words ending in the Tad. affixes signifying 'the child or the descendant', and to the words @deva[उक्षन्], @deva[उष्ट्र], @deva[उरभ्र] 'a ram', @deva[राजन्], @deva[राजन्य], @deva[राजपुत्र], @deva[वत्स], @deva[मनुष्य] and @deva[अज], it has the sense of 'a collection of'; @deva[उपगुनां समूहः औपगवकं] 'a number of the descendants of Upagu'; @deva[औक्षकं] 'a herd of cattle'; @deva[राजकं] 'a collection of kings', @deva[राजन्यकं] 'an assemblage of kshatriyas'; @deva[वात्सकं] 'a number of calves'; @deva[मानुष्यकं], @deva[अजकं] &c.;

**(11)** it is also added to @deva[क्रम], @deva[पद], @deva[शिक्षा], and @deva[मीमांसा] in the sense of 'one who has studied them'; @deva[क्रमकः] 'a student who goes through a regular course of study, or one who has studied the krama arrangement of a sacred text', @deva[मीमांसकः] 'a student of the mīmāṃsā philosophy', &c.

### @deva[वह्]

is added to the words @deva[पितृ] and @deva[मातृ] in the sense of 'the father of'; @deva[पितुः पिता पितामहः] 'a paternal grandfather'; @deva[मातामहः] 'a maternal grandfather'.

**(1)** @deva[उल] is added to @deva[मातृ] in the sense of 'the brother of'; @deva[मातुर्भ्राता मातुलः] ' a maternal uncle ';

**(2)** and @deva[व्य] is added to @deva[पितृ] and @deva[भ्रातृ] in the sense of ' the brother and the son of ' respectively ; @deva[पितुः भ्राता पितृव्यः] ' a paternal uncle '; @deva[भ्रातुः पुत्रः भ्रातृव्यः] ' a nephew.'

### @deva[आयन], @deva[इ]

And @deva[आयन], @deva[इ] are added to patronymics formed by means of Tad. affixes in the sense of 'the child of,' @deva[दाक्षायणः-पिः] ' the son of Dākshi '; @deva[गार्ग्यायणः-णिः] ' the son of @deva[गार्ग्य], a descendant of Garga '. @deva[आयन] is also added to the word @deva[कापिशी] ' name of a town ' in the sense of 'produced in'— @deva[कापिशायनः] , and optionally to @deva[द्रोण]; @deva[द्रोणायनः] or @deva[द्रौणिः] son of Drona.

### @deva[इ]

in the meaning of ' a son or a descendant of '; @deva[दाक्षिः] ' the son of Daksha '; @deva[वैयासकिः] ' the son of Vyāsa,' &c. ( In the case of the words @deva[व्यास], @deva[बह्व] ' name of a low caste,' @deva[विवाह], @deva[चण्डाल] and @deva[लिङ्ग], the final @deva[अ] is changed to @deva[आह्] before this @deva[इ]. )

### @deva[इ], @deva[ठञ्], @deva[ठन्]

has various senses:—

**(1)** @deva[रैवत्याः अपत्यं पुमान् रैवतिकः][^4] ' the son of Revati;

**(2)** ' happening or given once a month, monthly, lasting for a month ', &c. @deva[मासेन क्रीयते इति मासिकं वेतनं पुस्तकं वा]; similarly @deva[वार्षिकः भाटः] &c.

**(3)** ' gathering together ', @deva[सैनिकः];

**(4)** ' asking; ' @deva[स्नातं पृच्छतीति सौस्नातिकः] ' one who asks another whether he had an auspicious ablution '; so @deva[सुखसुप्तं पृच्छतीति सौसुखसुप्तिकः] ' one who asks another whether he had comfortable sleep '. ( see Rag. VI. 61 X. 14.); @deva[सौसहायिकः] &c ;

**(5)** ' using an instrument ', @deva[असिः प्रहरणमस्य असिकः] ' one who strikes with a sword, a swordsman '; @deva[धानुष्कः] ' an archer, '

**(6)** ' mixed with, ' &c.; @deva[दध्ना संसृष्टं दाधिकं] 'mixed with curds', @deva[मारीचिकं] fr. @deva[मरीचि] 'black pepper';

**(7)** @deva[धर्मे रत इति धार्मिकः] 'pious, religious', similarly @deva[अधार्मिकः].

**(8)** @deva[उड्डुपेन तरतीति नौपिकः] 'a boatman'; @deva[नाविकः] &c.

**(9)** @deva[हेष्टिना क्षरतीति हास्तिकः] 'one who rides an elephant'; @deva[शाकटेन क्षरतीति शाकटिकः] 'one who drives in a carriage';

**(10)** @deva[दध्ना भक्षयतीति दाधिकः] 'one who eats with curds';

**(11)** 'living upon' @deva[वेतनेन जीवतीति वैतनिकः] 'one who lives upon wages', so @deva[वाहनिकः], @deva[भोजवेदिकः] &c.

**(12)** 'carrying upon'; @deva[कटवेण हरतीति कौत्सङ्गिकः]

**(13)** @deva[अस्तीति बुद्धिः अस्य आस्तिकः] 'a believer in God and sacred writings'; @deva[नास्तिकः] &c.

**(14)** it is added to @deva[लाक्षा], @deva[रोचना], @deva[शाकल] and @deva[कर्दम] in the sense of 'dyed with', @deva[लाक्षया रक्तं लाक्षिकं] 'dyed with lac'. @deva[रोचनिकः], @deva[शाकलिकः] 'chequered or spotted', @deva[कार्दमिकः]।

**(15)** @deva[वेद], @deva[न्याय], @deva[श्रुति], @deva[लोकायत] and words ending in @deva[सूत्र] except @deva[कल्पसूत्र] &c.; in the sense of 'one who studies them'; @deva[वेदमधीते वैदिकः] 'a student of the Veda'; @deva[नैयायिकः] 'one who studies Nyāya or logic'; @deva[श्रुतिमधीते श्रौतिकः] 'one who studies a commentary' &c.; @deva[लौकायतिकः] 'an atheist, a student of the materialistic philosophy', @deva[सौत्रान्तिकः]; but @deva[कल्पसूत्रम्];

**(16)** to @deva[हस्तिन्], @deva[धेनु], @deva[केदार] and @deva[कवच] in the sense of 'a collection of'; @deva[हास्तिकं] 'a herd of elephants', @deva[धैनुकं] 'a herd of cows', @deva[केदारिकं] 'a collection of fields,' @deva[कवचिकं] 'a collection of armours';

**(17)** to @deva[अध्यात्मन्], @deva[अधिदैव], @deva[अधिभूत], @deva[इहलोक], @deva[परलोक], &c. in the sense of 'relating to &c.;' @deva[आत्मानमधिकृत्य भवः आध्यात्मिक] 'relating to the Supreme spirit', 'spiritual'; @deva[आधिदैविक] 'relating to or coming from the governing deity'. @deva[आधिभौतिकः] 'proceeding from the elements', @deva[ऐहलौकिकः] 'temporal', @deva[पारलौकिकः] &c.

**(18)** to @deva[क्रय], @deva[विक्रय], @deva[क्रयविक्रय], and @deva[वह] in the sense of 'living upon (in these cases no Vṛddhi substitute takes place); @deva[क्रयेण जीवतीति क्रयिकः] 'one who lives upon selling things, a trader', @deva[विक्रयिकः], @deva[वहिकः], 'one who lives upon wages'.

**(19)** to words denoting musical instruments in the sense of 'playing upon'; &c. @deva[मृदङ्गवादनं शिल्पमस्य मार्दङ्गिकः] 'one whose profession is to play on a tabor'; so @deva[वैणिकः] fr. Vīṇā; similarly @deva[वैणविकः]; @deva[मादुकः] or @deva[मादुकिकः]; @deva[झाल्लरिकः], &c.

**(20)** to @deva[पद्] and the remaining words[^5] of that group in the sense of 'walking with the assistance of;' @deva[पादिकः] [@deva[पदेन चरति इति, येन पदेन पद्भ्यामचरन्ति स पदः] Sid. Kan.]; @deva[अन्धेन चरति आन्धिकः], @deva[रथिकः] &c. @deva[पथा चरति पथिकः] 'a traveller'; this is also added to words denoting inanimate things. @deva[वारिपथिकं दारु] 'wood carried on by the force of water';

**(21)** to words included in the @deva[भस्त्रादि][^6] group in the sense of 'bears or carries by means of' @deva[भस्त्रया हरतीति भस्त्रिकः]; and to the word @deva[विश्वध]; @deva[विश्वधेन हरति विश्वधिकः]; also @deva[वैशधिकः]।

**(22)** to @deva[कुसीद] and @deva[दशैकादशन्] in the sense of 'lending on interest' @deva[कुसीदिकः] 'a usurer', @deva[दशैकादशिकः] 'one who lends another ten rupees in order to get back eleven i. e. 'a usurer'; and

**(23)** to @deva[आकर्ष]; @deva[आकर्षेण चरति आकर्षिकः] 'magnetic, attractive'.

### @deva[इन्]

( @deva[इणीय] ) Added to @deva[पूर्व] or words ending in @deva[पूर्व] and to @deva[श्राद्ध] it has the sense of 'done and eaten by' respectively; @deva[कृतपूर्वं कर्ता]; @deva[श्राद्धमनेन भुक्तं श्राद्धी] 'one who has eaten at a Śrāddha';

**(2)** it is added to a few words, such as @deva[खल], @deva[कोद्रव], &c. in the sense of 'a collection of' with fem. term. @deva[ई] added to it; @deva[खलानां समूहः खलिनी] 'a multitude of threshing floors or wicked men', @deva[कोद्रविनी] 'a number of families'. @deva[डाकिनी] ' a host of female goblins or imps,' @deva[डाकिनी], &c.

### @deva[इमन्] ( @deva[इमनिच्] )

forms abstract nouns when added to the words @deva[पृथु], @deva[वृड्], @deva[महत्] , @deva[तरु], @deva[पटु] @deva[लघु], @deva[बहु], @deva[साधु], @deva[आयु], @deva[उरु], @deva[गुरु],@deva[मृदु], @deva[खण्ड], @deva[दृढ], @deva[अकिञ्चन], @deva[वण्ड], @deva[बाल], @deva[बृहत्], @deva[होड], @deva[पाक], @deva[मन्द], @deva[स्वादु], @deva[ह्रस्व], @deva[दीर्घ], @deva[प्रिय], @deva[हृद्], @deva[क्षुध], @deva[शिश], @deva[क्षाट], @deva[अणु], @deva[हृद्], @deva[हृद्], @deva[परिवृढ], @deva[छात्र], @deva[धूम्र], @deva[भक्त], @deva[शीत], @deva[उष्ण], @deva[जड], @deva[वणिज्], @deva[मधुर], @deva[पण्डित], @deva[मूर्ख], @deva[मृज्], @deva[स्थिर], and words expressive of colour; before this term these undergo the same changes as before the @deva[ईयसु] of the comparative and are always mas.; as @deva[प्रथिमा] ' greatness', @deva[मृदिमा] 'softness ' @deva[तनिमा], ' thinness ' @deva[पटिमा] ' dexterity,' sharpness.' &c.; @deva[बालिमा], @deva[वलिमा], @deva[होडिमा], @deva[पाकिमा] 'childhood'; @deva[हसिमा], @deva[क्षोदिमा], @deva[दृढिमा], @deva[उष्णिमा], @deva[व्राडिमा], @deva[जडिमा], @deva[शुचिमा], &c.

### @deva[एय] ( @deva[एयञ्] )

this is added to

**(1)** @deva[क्षत्र] in the sense of born of the race of; @deva[क्षत्रियः];

**(2)** @deva[राष्ट्र] in the sense of ' relating to'; @deva[राष्ट्रियः];

**(3)** @deva[महेन्द्र] in the sense of ' an oblation offered to'; @deva[महेन्द्रियः होत्रः];

**(4)** @deva[अग्र]; @deva[अग्रियः] 'foremost.'

### @deva[ईक] ( @deva[ईकङ्] )

is added to @deva[शक्ति] and @deva[यष्टि] in the sense of ' striking with'; @deva[शक्त्या प्रहरतीति शाक्तीकः]; ' a spearman ' ( also @deva[शाक्तिकः] ); @deva[यष्टीकः] 'one who strikes with a stick'.

### @deva[ईन] ( @deva[छन्], @deva[खञ्] )

**(1)** added to @deva[कुल] and words ending in @deva[कुल] it means ' born of', @deva[कुले जातः कुलीनः] or @deva[कौलीनः] 'of a good family,' @deva[आढ्यकुलीनः—कौलीनः] 'sprung from a noble and rich family'; it is added to

**(2)** the words @deva[पार] and @deva[अपार] separately or taken together in any order in the sense of 'going'; as @deva[पारं गामीति पारीणः] 'going over to the other bank'. ( when used at the end of a comp. it means, versed or adept in; vide Bhaṭṭ; II.46 ). @deva[अपारीणः] 'coming over to this side ( of a river, &c.);' @deva[पारापारीणः] 'one who goes to both sides or one who crosses the sea': @deva[अपारपारीणः] 'crossing a river,' &c.

**(3)** the word @deva[ग्राम] in the sense of 'rustic' as @deva[ग्रामीणः];

**(4)** the words @deva[आत्मन्], @deva[विश्वजन] and words ending in @deva[भोग] in the sense of 'beneficial to;' @deva[आत्मने हितः आत्मनीनः]; @deva[विश्वजनीनः]; @deva[मातृभोगीयः] 'fit to be enjoyed by a mother'; @deva[पितृभोगीयः] &c.

**(5)** @deva[नु] changed to @deva[नु], as @deva[नवीनः];

**(6)** @deva[अध्वन्] in the sense of 'journeying' @deva[अध्वानं गच्छतीति अध्वनीनः] 'a traveller';

**(7)** @deva[सर्वान्न] and @deva[अनुपद्] in the senses of 'eating and fastended on' respectively, @deva[सर्वान्नीनः] 'eating every kind of food'; [^7]@deva[अनुपदे बद्धा अनुपदीना (उपानह्)] 'a shoe or boot of the length of the foot;

**(8)** @deva[तिल] and @deva[माष] in the sense of 'a field of'; as @deva[तैलीनं] 'a sesamum field', @deva[माषीणं], &c.; and to @deva[सप्तपद] and @deva[हिरण्य] substituted for @deva[पुरोगोदोह]; @deva[सप्तभिः पदैः अवाप्यते साप्तपदीनं] 'formed by walking together seven steps or speaking seven words'; @deva[हैरण्गवीनं][^8] 'fresh butter or ghee' (vide Rāg. 1. 45, Bhaṭṭi. V.12).

### @deva[ईय] ( @deva[ठक्] )

**(1)** is added in the sense of 'of or belonging to'; @deva[शालायाः अयं शालीयः] fr. @deva[शाला]: @deva[मालीयः] fr. @deva[माला]; @deva[पाणिनीयः] 'belonging to the school of Pāṇini'; it is added to

**(2)** @deva[स्वसृ] and @deva[पितृस्वसृ] and @deva[भ्रातृ] in the senses of 'the son of' and 'relating to,' respectively; @deva[स्वस्रीयः] 'a sister's son' @deva[पैतृस्वस्रीयः]; @deva[भ्रात्रीयः] 'fraternal';

**(3)** @deva[अश्व] in the sense of 'relating to or a number of' @deva[आश्वीयं] (also @deva[आश्व्यं]) 'relating to horses, a number of horses';

**(4)** when added to the words @deva[स्व], @deva[जन], @deva[पर्] @deva[देव], @deva[राजन्], @deva[वेणु] and @deva[वैध्य], @deva[क] is inserted, @deva[स्वकीयः] 'one's own,' @deva[जनकीयः] 'of the people' : @deva[परकीयः]. @deva[राजकीयः], @deva[वैणुकीयः], 'of a bamboo,' @deva[वैश्रकीयः]. @deva[वार्षिक्यः] 'produced in or relating to the rainy season,' fr. @deva[वार्षव].

### @deva[एय] ( @deva[एयञ्], @deva[एयच्], @deva[णेय्] )

is chiefly added

**(1)** to words ending in fem. affix in the sense of 'the child or offspring of'; @deva[वैनतेयः] 'the son of Vinatā i. e. Garuda'; @deva[भागिनेयः] 'the son of a sister'; when added to @deva[कुलटा] meaning 'a poor woman', @deva[इन] is inserted optionally. @deva[कौलटेयः] or @deva[कौलटिनेयः]; when @deva[कुलटा] means 'a harlot' or 'an adulteress' @deva[एर] is optionally substituted for @deva[एय]; @deva[कौलटेयः] or @deva[कौलटेरः] 'the son of an adulteress'; it is optionally changed to @deva[एर] when added to words denoting 'a female having some kind of defect', @deva[काणेय:-रः] 'son of a one-eyed woman,' @deva[दासेय:-रः] 'son of a female slave-';

**(2)** to words of two syllables ending in @deva[इ] but not formed by the affix @deva[इ] (@deva[इन्]), to @deva[मण्डूक] and words included in the @deva[शुभ्रादि] group[^9]; @deva[आत्रेयः] 'son of Atri', @deva[माण्डूकेयः] 'son of Māṇḍūka', @deva[शौभ्रेयः] 'son of Śubhra (Name of a sage), @deva[मैत्रेयः] &c.;

**(3)** and to @deva[मातृस्वसृ], and @deva[पितृस्वसृ], the final @deva[ऋ] being dropped before it; @deva[मातृस्वस्रेयः], @deva[पितृस्वस्रेयः],

**(4)** added to @deva[अग्नि] and @deva[कृति] it has various senses; @deva[आग्नेयः] 'son of Agni', 'relating to fire', 'having Agni for the presiding deity', &c.; it is affixed to

**(5)** @deva[नदी] and other words in the sense of 'produced from, &c.'; @deva[नद्यः इदं नद्यां भवं वा नादेयं] 'riverborn', 'rock-salt'; @deva[माहेयं] fr. @deva[मही] 'produced from the earth', @deva[वाराणसेयः] &c.;

**(6)** @deva[द्रोणि] and @deva[भाति] in the sense of 'a field of' @deva[द्रौणेयं], @deva[भातेयं];

**(7)** @deva[कुरु], @deva[कुस्ति], @deva[गीता], and words included in the @deva[कुण्डआदि] group[^10], with different significations and with a @deva[क] added to it; @deva[कौलेयकः] 'a dog', pertaining to a noble family'; @deva[कौशेयकः] 'a sword', @deva[शैवेयकः] 'a neck ornament', @deva[कृपितातः भयः कृपयः तव जातः काशेयकः], @deva[ग्रामेयकः], 'village-born, rustic'; @deva[नागरेयकः], &c.

**(8)** @deva[कोश] in the sense of 'made of'; @deva[कौशेयं] 'a silken garment';

**(9)** @deva[पुरुष] in different senses; @deva[पौरुषेयः] 'man-slaughter', 'human work', 'derived from or incidental to man, composed or propounded by man'; and

**(10)** to @deva[पथिन्], @deva[आतिथि], @deva[वसति] and @deva[स्वपति] in the sense of 'useful in, good for'; @deva[पथे साधु पाथेयं] 'what is useful on the way', i. e. 'provisions for a journey'; @deva[आतिथिषु साधुः आतिथेयः] 'attentive to guests, hospitable' @deva[वसौ साधुः वासतेयः] 'hospitable':—@deva[यं राशिः]; @deva[स्वपतेः गतं स्वपतेयं (धनं)] 'wealth, property'; vide Kir. XIV. 8.

### @deva[क]

is affixed

**(1)** to words expressive of countries in the sense of 'born or produced in'; @deva[माद्रकः] 'born or produced in the Madra country';

**(2)** to @deva[पीत] in the sense of 'dyed with'; @deva[पीतकः] 'dyed yellow';

**(3)** in the sense of 'belonging to'; @deva[माद्रकः], @deva[स्वकः], &c.

**(4)** 'bought for' @deva[पञ्चकः] 'bought for five rupees';

**(5)** in the sense of 'acting' @deva[शीतकः] 'one who is cold' i. e. 'slow in action,' 'a dilatory or lazy man;' @deva[उष्णकः] 'an active man';

**(6. 7. 8.)** to express pity or diminution, or depreciation-@deva[पुत्रकः] 'poor son' @deva[देवदत्तकः] 'unhappy Devadatta'; @deva[ह्रस्वो वृक्षो वृक्षकः], 'a small or stunted tree'; @deva[अश्वकः] a bad horse, a hack; @deva[शूद्रकः] 'a wicked Sudra,'

**(9)** and sometimes with no signification; @deva[अविकः] i. e. @deva[अविः] 'a ram' @deva[मणिकः] 'a jewel', @deva[बालकः] 'a young boy'; &c

### @deva[ग] ( @deva[वुञ्] )

is affixed

**(1)** to words denoting names of beasts, in the sense of 'a collection of'; @deva[अविकुञ्जं] 'a flock of sheep'

