## Dropping of Penultimate Nasal in Benedictive

A penultimate nasal is generally dropped. Some of the roots dropping their nasal thus are:

@deva[भञ्ज], @deva[अञ्ज], @deva[वञ्ज], @deva[रञ्ज], @deva[सञ्ज], @deva[रुञ्ज], @deva[युञ्ज], @deva[मुञ्ज], @deva[उञ्च], @deva[स्कन्द्], @deva[स्यन्द्], @deva[इञ्ज], @deva[वृञ्ज], @deva[स्तम्भ], @deva[सिञ्ज], @deva[शुङ्ग], @deva[शुम्भ], @deva[अञ्च] and @deva[तुङ्ग].

## Final Vowel Changes to @deva[ए] in Benedictive

@deva[दा], @deva[धा] and roots assuming these forms, @deva[मा], @deva[स्था], @deva[गै], @deva[पा] 'to drink', @deva[हा] 'to abandon' and @deva[सो], change their final to @deva[ए].

Final @deva[आ] (original or substituted; see @ref[459]), if it be preceded by a conjunct consonant, is changed to @deva[ए] optionally.

**Examples:**
- @deva[दा]—@deva[देयात्]
- @deva[पा]—@deva[पेयात्]
- @deva[गै]—@deva[गेयात्]
- @deva[ग्ला]—@deva[ग्लेयात्], @deva[ग्लायात्] &c.

@note[type=exception]{@deva[पा] to 'protect', @deva[पायात्].}

**Ātmanepada.**

## Special Cases: @deva[ई] and @deva[ऊह्] in Benedictive

@deva[ई] 'to go'—@deva[ईयासम्]; but shortens its @deva[ई] after a preposition, @deva[समियासम्]; Ātm. @deva[एषीय].

@deva[ऊह्] also, when joined with prepositions, shortens its @deva[ऊ] before weak terminations beginning with @deva[य]; @deva[संहूयासम्].

