**SECTION II.**

**THE PASSIVE**

## Formation of Desiderative Base by Reduplication

The Desiderative base is formed by reduplicating the root or base according to the general rules of reduplication given at @ref[444]-@ref[449] and @ref[549] (a) (b), and by adding @deva[स्] (which may by changed to @deva[ष्] according to the rules of Sandhi) to it. The @deva[अ] of the reduplicative syllable is changed to @deva[इ].

**Example:**
@deva[पठ्]—@deva[पपठ्]—@deva[पिपठ्] + @deva[स] = @deva[पिपठिष्] by the following rule.

@note[type=note]{The @deva[स्] of a primitive root is not changed to @deva[ष्] when the characteristic @deva[स्] is changed to @deva[ष्]; @deva[सि]—@deva[सिसीष्], @deva[सिच्]—@deva[सिसिक्ष्] (@deva[क] + @deva[ष]); @deva[स्मि]—@deva[सिस्मयिष्]; @deva[सु]—@deva[सुषूष्]; but @deva[स्था]—@deva[तिष्ठास्]; @deva[सावय्] cau. of @deva[सू]—@deva[सुषावयिष्]; @deva[स्तु], however, forms @deva[तुष्टूषति].}

@note[type=note]{A root takes a Desiderative form only when the agent of the wish and of the action expressed by the root is the same; so @deva[शिष्याः पठन्तु इति इच्छति गुरु] and not @deva[पिपाठयिषति]; also the sense of the root must be the object of the wish: @deva[गमनेन इच्छति] cannot, therefore, be equal to @deva[जिगमिषति].}

@note[type=note]{Though the Desiderative form of a root is not to be found often used in classical language in its character of a verb, yet nominal and participal derivatives from it are not uncommonly to be met with.}

## Conjugation of Desiderative Base in Conjugational Tenses

@deva[अ] is added to the base in the Conjugational Tenses and then it is conjugated like the special base of the 6th class in the Active and Passive.

**Non-Conjugational Tenses.**

## Formation of Ātmanepada Frequentative Base

The Ātm. Frequentative base is formed by adding @deva[य] to the root, before which it undergoes the same changes as before the @deva[य] of the Passive:

@deva[भू]—@deva[भूय], @deva[ऋ]—@deva[ईर्य], @deva[जि]—@deva[जीय], @deva[शी]—@deva[शीय], @deva[भू]—@deva[भूय], @deva[सू]—@deva[स्वय], @deva[ऋ]—@deva[अर्थ], @deva[दू]—@deva[कीर्य], @deva[पे]—@deva[धीय], etc.; @deva[निह्]—@deva[निष्य], @deva[तृ]—@deva[तूर्य], @deva[खण्ड्]—@deva[खन्दय], @deva[नस्त्र]—@deva[नश्य], etc.

### (a) Special Vowel Changes

@deva[ज्ञा] and @deva[स्मा] change their vowel to @deva[ई], and @deva[ऋ] preceded by one radical consonant is changed to @deva[ऊ], and not to @deva[ऋ]:

@deva[ज्ञा]—@deva[ज्ञीय], @deva[स्मा]—@deva[स्मीय], @deva[कृ]—@deva[कूर्य]

### (b) Samprasāraṇa and Substitutions

The roots @deva[सघुत्], @deva[समुद्], @deva[स्मर्], @deva[स्वप्], @deva[मृड्], @deva[मञ्चु], @deva[मस्त्र] and @deva[गुञ्ज्] take Samprasāraṇa.

@deva[हु] and @deva[हु] substitute @deva[ई] for their final vowel.

@deva[सरिट्] substitutes @deva[जिर्] and @deva[व्याद्] @deva[री]:

@deva[सघुत्]—@deva[निच्], @deva[स्पर्]—@deva[हन्य], @deva[मुड्]—@deva[युन्], @deva[हे]—@deva[इय], @deva[ज्ञा]—@deva[ज्ञीय], @deva[साद्]—@deva[मिल्य], @deva[व्याद्]—@deva[पीन्]

### (c) Additional Rule

@ref[395] should be observed.

## Nasal Insertion in Ātmanepada Frequentatives

When a root ends in a nasal preceded by @deva[अ] and the nasal is not dropped, @deva[व] (changeable to an Anusvāra or the nasal of the class to which the letter following it belongs) is inserted between the reduplicative @deva[अ] and the first radical consonant; the @deva[अ] of the reduplicative syllable thus remains unchanged (against @ref[629] b.).

### Examples

@deva[गम्]—@deva[गम्य]: @deva[नयम्यते] or @deva[नङ्गम्यते]

@deva[जन्]—@deva[जन्य]: @deva[वंजन्यते] or @deva[जञ्जन्यते]

But when @deva[जन्] = @deva[ज्ञातुं], the Ā. Freq. base is @deva[जाजाय], 3rd sing. @deva[जाजायते]

### (a) Extended Application

The same rule applies to the roots @deva[चर्], @deva[फण्], @deva[गुप्], @deva[जप्], @deva[वंद्], @deva[दंश्], @deva[मञ्ज्] and @deva[पद्].

@deva[चर्] and @deva[फण्] after inserting @deva[व्] change the @deva[अ] of the following syllable to @deva[अ]:

@deva[चर्]—@deva[चर्य]—@deva[वचर्य] = @deva[वचर्यते] or @deva[अचर्यते]; or @deva[चञ्चूर्यते] by @ref[694]

@deva[फण्] = @deva[फल्य] = @deva[वफञ्चयते] or @deva[पेफुल्यते] or @deva[पफूल्यते]

@deva[वंद्] = @deva[वद्]—@deva[वद्य] = @deva[ववद्यते] or @deva[ववन्द्वयते]

@deva[वुग्]—@deva[वञ्गयते] or @deva[वङ्गायते]

## Insertion of @deva[री] in Ātmanepada Frequentatives with Penultimate @deva[ऋ]

When a root contains a penultimate @deva[ऋ] (@deva[ऌ]) original or brought in by Samprasāraṇa, the syllable @deva[री] is inserted between the @deva[अ] of the reduplicative syllable (which remains short against @ref[629] b) and the radical consonant:

@deva[वृत्] = @deva[वृत्य] = @deva[ववृत्य] = @deva[वरीवृत्यते]

@deva[प्रच्छ्] = @deva[पृच्छ्य] = @deva[परीपृच्छ्यते]

@deva[नृत्] = @deva[नरीनृत्यते]

@deva[गृह्] = @deva[जरीगृह्यते]

