**Conjugation of the Ātm. Freq. Base**

## Reduplication in Parasmaipada Frequentatives

The root is reduplicated according to the general rules of reduplication; the vowels @deva[इ] and @deva[उ] in the reduplicative syllable take their guṇa substitute, and the @deva[अ] of the reduplicative syllable is lengthened:

@deva[भू]—@deva[बोभू]

@deva[चो]—@deva[नौच]

@deva[दिव्]—@deva[देदिव्], etc.

@deva[वच्]—@deva[वोवच्]

@deva[पू]—@deva[पोपू]—@deva[पापू]

@deva[विद्]—@deva[विवद्]—@deva[वेविद्]

@deva[डुय्]—@deva[डुयड्]—@deva[डोयुड्], etc.

## Extension of § 630 Rules to Parasmaipada Frequentatives

The rules @ref[630] (a) (b) apply likewise to the Parasm. Frequentative Base:

@deva[चर्]—@deva[वंचर्] or @deva[वैचर्]

@deva[वद्]—@deva[वंवद्] or @deva[वंवद्]

@deva[वञ्ज्]—@deva[वंवोञ्ज्], etc.

## Insertion of @deva[र्], @deva[रि], or @deva[री] in Parasmaipada Frequentatives

@deva[र्] or the syllable @deva[रि] or @deva[री] is inserted between the @deva[अ] of the reduplicative syllable and the radical consonant of roots ending in short @deva[ऋ] or having it for their penultimate.

Similarly @deva[ल्] or @deva[लि] or @deva[ली] is inserted in the case of @deva[कृप्]:

@deva[वृत्] = @deva[ववृत्]—@deva[वर्वृत्] or @deva[वरिवृत्] or @deva[वरीवृत्]

@deva[कृ]—@deva[चर्कृ], or @deva[चरिकृ] or @deva[चरीकृ]

@deva[कृप्]—@deva[चल्कृप्], or @deva[चलिकृप्] or @deva[चलीकृप्]

@deva[दृश्]—@deva[दर्दृश्], @deva[दरिदृश्] or @deva[दरीदृश्]

---

**Conjugation of the Parasm. Freq. Base**

## Semantic Distinction in Parasmaipada Frequentatives

As the Parasm. Freq. base is used both in the sense of frequency and of intensity, it has been said to denote the former in the strong cases and the latter in the weak.

### Examples

@deva[जोहूति], @deva[जोहवीति] 'to invoke frequently'

@deva[जुहुती] 'to invoke repeatedly'

It is, however, not easy to make such a distinction with regard to the other roots.

## Vowel Changes Before @deva[य] in Nominal Verbs

Before this @deva[य]:

### (1) Final @deva[अ] and @deva[आ] → @deva[ई]

@deva[पुत्रं आत्मनः इच्छति]—@deva[पुत्रीयति] (@deva[पुत्र] + @deva[य] = @deva[पुत्री] + @deva[य] + @deva[ति]) 'he wishes for a son'

### (2) Final @deva[इ] and @deva[उ] are Lengthened

@deva[कवि]—@deva[कवीयति] 'he wishes for a poet'

### (3) Final @deva[ऋ] → @deva[री]

@deva[कर्तृ]—@deva[कर्तरीयति]

### (4) Final @deva[ओ] and @deva[औ] → @deva[अव्] and @deva[आव्]

@deva[गो]—@deva[गव्यति]

@deva[नौ]—@deva[नाव्यति]

### (5) Final Nasal Dropped, Preceding Vowel Changed

A final nasal is dropped and the preceding vowel is changed like an original final vowel:

@deva[राजन्]—@deva[राजीयति] 'he wishes for a king'

### (6) Other Final Consonants Unchanged

In other cases the final consonant remains unchanged:

@deva[वाच्]—@deva[वाच्यति] 'he wishes for words'

@deva[दिव्]—@deva[दिव्यति] (@deva[दीव्यति] according to some) 'he wishes for heaven'

@deva[समिध्]—@deva[समिध्यति] 'he wishes for holy sticks', &c.

### (7) Taddhita Affix Dropped

The Tad. affix expressing 'a descendant of' is dropped and then the changes mentioned above take place:

@deva[गार्ग्य] (the son of @deva[गर्ग]) @deva[आत्मनः इच्छति]—@deva[गार्गीयति] (@deva[गार्ग्य] + @deva[य] + @deva[ति] = @deva[गार्ग] + @deva[य] + @deva[ति] = @deva[गार्गी] + @deva[य] + @deva[ति]), &c.

## Insertion of @deva[स्] and @deva[अस्] in Nominal Verbs

The consonant @deva[स्] and the syllable @deva[अस्] are inserted between any nominal stem and the affix @deva[य]:

@deva[मधु आत्मन इच्छति]—@deva[मधुस्यति] or @deva[मधवस्यति] 'he wishes for honey'

So @deva[दधिस्यति], @deva[दध्यस्यति], &c.

Final @deva[अ] is dropped before @deva[अस्]: @deva[पुत्रस्यति]

### (a) Special Cases with @deva[अस्] Insertion

@deva[अस्] is inserted:

- After @deva[वृष] and @deva[अश्व] when the sense to be conveyed is that of longing for them
- After @deva[क्षीर] and @deva[लवण] when the one is desired to be drunk and the other to be licked

#### Examples

@deva[वृषस्यति गौः] 'the cow longs for the ox'

@deva[अश्वस्यति वडवा] 'the mare longs for the horse'

@deva[क्षीरस्यति बालः] 'the child desires to drink'

@deva[लवणस्यति उष्ट्रः] 'the camel wishes for licking the salt'

But: @deva[वृषीयति] 'he desires to have a bull', @deva[अश्वीयति] 'he wishes for a horse', @deva[क्षीरीयति], @deva[लवणीयति]

## Restriction on @deva[य] Affix with @deva[स्]-Ending Nouns

The affix @deva[य] is not added to nouns ending in @deva[स्] and to indeclinables:

@deva[कामिच्छति], @deva[स्वरिच्छति] 'he longs for heaven'

## Non-Desiderative Uses of @deva[य] Nominal Verbs

This form of the Nominal verb has not always a desiderative meaning.

### (a) Treating or Considering Like

The affix @deva[य] is added in the sense of 'treating or considering like':

@deva[पुत्रीयति छात्रम्] 'he treats the pupil as a son'

@deva[विष्णूयति द्विजम्] 'he treats the Brāhmaṇa like Vishṇu'

@deva[प्रासादीयति कुट्यां भिक्षुः] 'the beggar considers his hut a palace'

@deva[कुटीयति प्रासादे राजा] 'the king in his palace considers himself to be in a hut'

### (b) Specific Uses

It is added to @deva[नमस्], @deva[वरिवस्] and @deva[चित्र] in the senses of 'adoring', 'serving' and 'striking with wonder' respectively:

@deva[नमस्यति देवान्] 'he adores the gods'

@deva[वरिवस्यति गुरुम्] 'he serves the preceptor'

@deva[चित्रीयते लोकान्] 'he strikes the people with wonder'

It is also added to @deva[तपस्] in the sense of 'practising': @deva[तपस्यति]

## Formation with @deva[काम्य] Affix

To express the sense of wishing for that which is denoted by the noun, the affix @deva[काम्य] is also added like the above and the base so derived conjugated in the Parasmaipada as before.

### Examples

@deva[पुत्रकाम्यति] 'he wishes for a son'

@deva[यशस्काम्यति] 'he wishes for fame'

@deva[सर्पिष्काम्यति] 'he wishes for ghee'

## Vowel Changes in Nominal Verbs Formed Without an Affix

The penultimate @deva[अ] of a noun ending in a nasal is lengthened. The base is treated like a root of the 1st conjugation, its last vowel only taking Guṇa before this @deva[अ]:

### Examples

@deva[अ] (name of Vishṇu) @deva[इव आचरति]—@deva[अति] 'he acts like Vishṇu'

@deva[कृष्ण]—@deva[कृष्णति] 'he acts like @deva[कृष्ण]' (@deva[कृष्णामि] 1st sing.)

@deva[कवि]—@deva[कवयामि] 'I act the poet or behave like a poet'

@deva[वि]—@deva[वयति] 'he behaves like a bird'

@deva[माला]—@deva[मालाति] 'he or it acts like a garland' (Perf. @deva[मालांच], &c.)

@deva[पितृ]—@deva[पितरति] 'he acts like a father'

@deva[भू]—@deva[भवति] 'acts like the earth' (Perf. @deva[बुभाव], &c. as @deva[भू] is the base)

@deva[राजन्]—@deva[राजानति] 'he acts like a king'

@deva[पथिन्]—@deva[पथीनति] 'it serves as a road', &c.

So @deva[इदामति] from @deva[इदम्], @deva[ऋभुक्षीणाति] from @deva[ऋभुक्षिन्] (name of Indra)

### (b) Optional Affixes

The words @deva[अवगलभ] (a bold man), @deva[होड] (a child) and @deva[क्लीब] take the affixes @deva[क्यङ्] and @deva[क्विप्] optionally and are conjugated in the Ātmanepada:

@deva[अवगलभते] or @deva[अवगलभायते]

@deva[होडते] or @deva[होडायते]

@deva[क्लीबते] or @deva[क्लीबायते]

---

### (d) By means of the affix @deva[य] (@deva[क्यङ्]) and conjugated in the Ātm.

## Vowel Changes Before @deva[क्यङ्]

Before this affix the final @deva[अ] of a nominal base is lengthened, @deva[आ] remains unchanged, other final letters undergo the same changes as they do before the other @deva[य] (@deva[क्यच्]).

The final @deva[स्] of a noun is changed to @deva[आ] optionally and that of @deva[अप्सरस्] and @deva[ओजस्] necessarily.

### Examples

@deva[कृष्ण इव आचरति]—@deva[कृष्णायते] 'he acts like Kṛṣṇa'

@deva[यशस्]—@deva[यशायते], @deva[यशस्यते] 'he behaves like one who is famous'

@deva[विद्वस्]—@deva[विद्वायते], @deva[विद्वस्यते] 'he acts like a learned man', &c.

But @deva[ओजस्]—@deva[ओजायते] 'acts like one who is lustrous' (powerful)

@deva[अप्सरस्]—@deva[अप्सरायते] 'she behaves like an Apsaras'

### (a) Feminine Nouns

A feminine noun not having @deva[ऋ] for its penultimate drops its feminine termination:

@deva[कुमारीव आचरति]—@deva[कुमारायते] 'he behaves like a girl'

@deva[हरिणीव आचरति]—@deva[हरिणायते] 'she acts like a female deer'

@deva[युवतीव आचरति]—@deva[युवत्यते] 'acts like a stout woman'

But @deva[पाचिका इव आचरति]—@deva[पाचिकायते] 'she acts like a female cook', and not @deva[पाचकायते]

### (b) Special Forms of @deva[सपत्नी] and @deva[युवति]

@deva[सपत्नी] has @deva[सपत्नायते], @deva[सपत्नीयते] and @deva[सपतीयते] 'she acts like a co-wife'; @deva[युवति] has @deva[युवायते] 'she behaves like a young woman.'

## @deva[य] Affix for 'Becoming What It Was Not Before'

The affix @deva[य] is added to a few nouns such as @deva[भृश] 'much', @deva[मन्द] 'slow', @deva[पण्डित] 'learned', @deva[सुमनस्] 'generous-minded', @deva[उन्मनस्] 'agitated', &c. in the sense of 'becoming what it was not before', or 'what it was not like to before':

### Examples

@deva[भृशः भवति]—@deva[भृशायते] 'what was not much now becomes much'

@deva[उन्मनायते] 'he (who was not agitated before) becomes agitated'

Similarly @deva[सुमनायते], &c.

## Special Uses of @deva[क्यङ्] Affix

The following are the different senses in which the affix @deva[क्यङ्] is used in the particular cases given below.

### (a) Desirous of Committing Sin

It is added to @deva[सत्र], @deva[कष्ट], @deva[कृच्छ्र] and @deva[गहन] in the sense of 'desirous of committing sin':

@deva[पापं चिकीर्षति]—@deva[सत्रायते], @deva[कष्टायते], &c.

Added to @deva[कष्ट] it has also the sense of 'prompt in': @deva[कष्टाय क्रमते]—@deva[कष्टायते] (@deva[पापं कर्तुमुत्सहते इत्यर्थः], Sid. Kau.)

### (b) Ruminating

To @deva[रोमन्थ] used objectively: @deva[रोमन्थायते] 'is ruminating'

### (c) Sending Forth, Vomiting

To @deva[बाष्प] 'tears', @deva[ऊष्मन्] 'heat', and @deva[फेन], in the sense of 'sending forth, vomiting':

@deva[बाष्पायते] 'he sheds tears'

@deva[ऊष्मायते] 'gives out heat'

@deva[फेनायते] 'sends forth foam'

### (d) Experiencing or Enjoying

To @deva[सुख] and others in the sense of 'experiencing or enjoying':

@deva[सुखं वेदयते]—@deva[सुखायते] 'he enjoys happiness'

But @deva[परस्य सुखं वेदयते] 'he shows the happiness of another'

### (e) Making or Doing

To @deva[शब्द], @deva[वैर], @deva[कलह], @deva[अभ्र], @deva[कण्व] 'sin', @deva[सुदिन] 'a fair day', @deva[दुर्दिन] 'a cloudy day' and @deva[नीहार] 'fog, heavy dew', in the sense of 'making or doing':

@deva[शब्दं करोति]—@deva[शब्दायते] 'he makes a sound' (also @deva[शब्दयति] cau.)

@deva[सुदिनायते], &c.

---

### (e) By means of the affix @deva[क्यष्] (@deva[य]) and conjugated in Parasm. and Ātm.

## Formation with @deva[इ] Affixes (@deva[णिङ्] and @deva[णिच्])

Verbal bases are formed from the nouns given below by the addition of the affixes @deva[इ] (@deva[णिङ्]), and @deva[इ] (@deva[णिच्]) with various senses.

Those derived by means of @deva[णिङ्] are conjugated in the Ātmanepada and those by @deva[णिच्] in the Parasmaipada.

### Examples

@deva[पुच्छं] with @deva[वि], @deva[उद्], and @deva[परि]—@deva[उत्पुच्छयते] 'raises the tail,' @deva[विपुच्छयते], @deva[परिपुच्छयते]

@deva[सम्भाण्डयते] 'collects together the vessels'

@deva[सञ्चीवरयते भिक्षुः] 'the mendicant collects together or wears tattered garments'

@deva[मुण्ड]—@deva[मुण्डयति माणवकम्] 'he shaves Māṇavaka'

@deva[मिश्र]—@deva[मिश्रयति अन्नम्] 'he mixes boiled rice with (curds, curry, &c.)'

@deva[श्लक्ष्ण]—@deva[श्लक्ष्णयति वस्त्रम्] 'he weaves cloth of a very thin texture'

@deva[लवणयति व्यञ्जनम्] 'mixes salt with condiments'

@deva[व्रतयति पयः] 'he observes the vow of living upon milk only'

## Change of @deva[इङ्] to @deva[आकिङ्]

@deva[इङ्] is changed to @deva[आकिङ्] when added to @deva[सत्य], @deva[अर्थ] and @deva[वर्ण]:

@deva[सत्यं करोति आत्मनं वा]—@deva[सत्याकिङ्गति]

@deva[अर्थाकिङ्गति]

@deva[वर्णाकिङ्गति]

## Additional Uses of @deva[इङ्] Affix

@deva[इङ्] is further added in the following cases:

@deva[काणेन अभियान]—@deva[आभीकणाकिङ्गति]

@deva[लाता अदुभाट]—@deva[अदुभाकिङ्गति]

@deva[काणेन उपगायत]—@deva[उपकाणाकिङ्गति]

@deva[भूतिके शूपस्तोति]—@deva[उपभूतिकाकिङ्गति]

@deva[तट् यूव्वाति]—@deva[तट्यति]

@deva[पाणीज्]—@deva[पाणीजीकिङ्गति]

@deva[निवातवते]—@deva[निवाते] 'clears the air of vapours'

@deva[चूर्णाकिङ्गति]

@deva[एनीयाजेडे]—@deva[एनयते] 'declares her variegated', etc.

The various changes taking place here before the affix @deva[य] the student will easily notice as irregularities.

---

### (g) By means of the affix @deva[य] (@deva[यङ्])

## Expressing Desire by Adding Root to Root

The notion of 'desiring' is expressed by adding a root to a root:

### Examples

'to eat salt': @deva[लवणप्यति] = @deva[लवण] + @deva[यु], @deva[यु] meaning 'to take' or 'to desire'

Similarly:

@deva[पुष्पयति]

@deva[लवणगृह्यति] = @deva[लवण] + @deva[गृह्]

@deva[सुकर्षति], etc.

## Special Forms of @deva[आन] Participles

### (a) Change to @deva[इ]

The @deva[आ] of @deva[आन] is changed to @deva[इ] in the case of the root @deva[आस्] (2 cl.) 'to sit':

Present Participle: @deva[आसीन]

### (b) Formation of Nouns

@deva[आन] added to the roots @deva[पू] and @deva[यज्] forms nouns:

@deva[पवमानः] 'that which purifies, hence, the wind' (cf. Rag. VIII. 9); also, 'one of the sacred fires'

@deva[यजमानः] 'one who sacrifices'

## Extended Use of @deva[आन] for Habit and Capacity

The termination @deva[आन] may be added to any root in the sense of 'in the habit of' or 'to show a particular standard of age, or capacity to do a thing':

### Examples

@deva[भोगं भुञ्जानः] 'one habituated to enjoy pleasures'

@deva[कवचं बिभ्राणः] 'of a sufficient age, i.e. young enough to bear armour'

@deva[शत्रुं निघ्नानः] 'able to kill the enemy', etc.

## Irregular Perfect Participles from @deva[ऋ]-Ending Roots

Roots ending in @deva[ऋ] (@deva[ऋ] and @deva[लृ] included) form their Perfect Participle irregularly.

### Parasmaipada Formation

@deva[वस्] is added to the root, which then undergoes the changes mentioned in @ref[394], and is finally reduplicated.

### Ātmanepada Formation

When a root is Ātmanepada it is first reduplicated and @deva[आन] afterwards added, the final @deva[ऋ] changing as before.

### Examples

@deva[कृ] + @deva[वस्] = @deva[कीर्वस्], by reduplication @deva[चिकीर्वस्]

@deva[कृ]—by reduplication @deva[चक्र्] + @deva[आन] = @deva[चाकिराण]

Similarly:

@deva[तॄ]—@deva[तितीर्वस्], @deva[ततिराण]

@deva[शॄ]—@deva[शिशीर्वस्], @deva[शशिराण]

@deva[पॄ]—@deva[पुपूर्वस्], @deva[पपुराण], etc.

@deva[हन्] takes the affix @deva[यत्] optionally, before which @deva[वध्] is substituted for it; @deva[हन्+य=वध्यः]='what ought to be killed,' it optionally takes @deva[एयत्], in which case @deva[घात्] is substituted for it; @deva[घात्यः].

---

**By means of the affix @deva[क्यप्] (@deva[य])**

@deva[युज्] in the sense of 'to be harnessed' takes the affix @deva[क्यप्] and changes its final to @deva[ग्]; @deva[युग्यः गौः] 'a bull to be harnessed to the yoke;' in other sense it takes the affix @deva[त्]; @deva[युक्तः].

---

**By means of the affix @deva[घ्यत्].**

## Root @deva[विश्] with @deva[अभि] and @deva[आ]: Accusative and Locative

@deva[विश्] with @deva[अभि] governs the Accusative; @deva[अभिनिविशते सुभगं मार्गं] he pursues the path of goodness; @deva[सुभगा सा गणिका यस्यां भवन्मनः अभिनिविशते] happy is that harlot girl on whom you have fixed your mind (see Bhaṭṭi. VIII, 80,).

Rarely this governs the Loc. @deva[अभिनिविशते पापं] fondly resorts to sin. @deva[विश्] with a preposition governs the Acc. but with @deva[आ] meaning 'to sit' takes the Loc. @deva[अत्र आसनं आविशत] sit on this seat.

## Roots Governing Double Accusative

The roots given in the following Kārikā govern a double Accusative—

@deva[दुह्माप्यच्प्रच्छिचिब्रूशासजिमथस्तुयः ।]
@deva[कर्माक्रियोः तथा स्थानेऽक्रियायां च वा ॥]

i.e. the roots @deva[दुह्] to milk, @deva[पच्] to cook, @deva[याच्] to punish, @deva[प्रच्छ्] to obstruct, @deva[छि] to ask, @deva[चि] to collect, @deva[ब्रू] to speak, @deva[शास्] to instruct, @deva[जि] to win (as a wager), @deva[मथ्] to churn, and @deva[स्तु] to steal, as also @deva[क्री], @deva[कृ] and @deva[नी] and @deva[हृ]; @deva[गां दुग्धं दोहे] he milks (draws milk from) the cow, @deva[बलिं वसुधां याचते बलिः] he begs the earth of Bali; @deva[तण्डुलान् ओदनं पचति] he cooks rice (into food); similarly @deva[मागान् दण्डं दण्डयति. ब्राह्मणान् भो. मार्गं प्रच्छति. वस्तु अवचिनोति कृती. मार्गं वनं द्विते शास्ति, चतुर्थं दैन्यतं, नी चतुर्थतरं मनुष्यते. द्वितं हरिं मथ्यति, मामरातनं नयति कृती चतुति नः] So @deva[मार्गं धर्मं मनुते याचते वा, बलिं चङ्गां निश्चते], &c. Vide Bhaṭṭi. VI, 8–10

The following stanza from the Bhaṭṭi Kāvya illustrates the uses of some of these interjections:—

@deva[आहः कुयूकुयूं वनु हो चिदुयूनुयूं हू युयूदैयुयूनुत्तुयुयूति ऐक्तुयु ।]
@deva[हुयू यिनुयुः कुयूरुयि हं शुयूदै वुदुयुनुयूयूं निजुयूलुयु संयु ॥]
